The Security Council,

Expressing its firm commitment to the sovereignty, independence, unity and territorial integrity of the Bolivarian Republic of Venezuela,

Reaffirming the purposes and principles of the Charter of the United Nations, in particular Article 2, paragraph 4, and Article 2, paragraph 7,

Expressing concern over attempts to intervene in matters which are essentially within the domestic jurisdiction of any State,

Expressing concern also over threats to use force against the territorial integrity and political independence of the Bolivarian Republic of Venezuela,

Reaffirming General Assembly resolution 46/182 of 19 December 1991, which establishes that humanitarian assistance should be provided with the consent of the affected country and in principle on the basis of an appeal by the affected country, and that the sovereignty, territorial integrity and national unity of States must be fully respected in accordance with the Charter of the United Nations,

Recalling that the Government of the Bolivarian Republic of Venezuela has the primary responsibility for initiating, organizing, coordinating, and implementing humanitarian assistance within its territory,

Welcoming and supporting initiatives aimed at facilitating a peaceful, political and negotiated solution among Venezuelans, including the Montevideo Mechanism established on 7 February 2019,

1. Urges the settlement of the current situation in the Bolivarian Republic of Venezuela exclusively through peaceful means, within the framework of its national Constitution and in full respect of its sovereignty;

2. Supports all initiatives aimed at reaching a political solution among Venezuelans, through a genuine, inclusive and comprehensive process of national dialogue;

3. Calls for the facilitation of peaceful and unhindered delivery of humanitarian assistance across the entire territory of the Bolivarian Republic of Venezuela, in accordance with the fundamental humanitarian principles of humanity, neutrality, impartiality and independence, and with the consent and coordination of the Government of the Bolivarian Republic of Venezuela;

4. Reaffirms the primary role of the Government of the Bolivarian Republic of Venezuela in the initiation, organization, coordination and implementation of humanitarian assistance efforts and initiatives within its territory;

5. Decides to remain seized of the matter.

