Recalling that the Government of the Bolivarian Republic of Venezuela has the primary responsibility for initiating, organizing, coordinating, and implementing humanitarian assistance within its territory,

Welcoming and supporting initiatives aimed at facilitating a peaceful, political and negotiated solution among Venezuelans, including the Montevideo Mechanism established on 7 February 2019, and taking note of other initiatives aimed at promoting dialogue,

1. Urges the settlement of the current situation in the Bolivarian Republic of Venezuela exclusively through peaceful means, within the framework of its national Constitution and in full respect of its sovereignty;

2. Supports all initiatives aimed at reaching a political solution among Venezuelans, through a genuine, inclusive, Venezuelan-led and Venezuelan-owned comprehensive process of national dialogue, and calls upon all Venezuelan political actors to engage constructively without delay to achieve a peaceful and consensual outcome;

3. Calls for the facilitation of peaceful and unhindered delivery of humanitarian assistance across the entire territory of the Bolivarian Republic of Venezuela, in accordance with the fundamental humanitarian principles of humanity, neutrality, impartiality and independence, stresses that humanitarian assistance must remain strictly depoliticized, and reaffirms that such assistance must be provided with the consent and coordination of the Government of the Bolivarian Republic of Venezuela;

4. Reaffirms the primary role of the Government of the Bolivarian Republic of Venezuela in the initiation, organization, coordination and implementation of humanitarian assistance efforts and initiatives within its territory;

5. Decides to remain seized of the matter.

